  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ナガミハマナタマメ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8A%E3%82%AC%E3%83%9F%E3%83%8F%E3%83%9E%E3%83%8A%E3%82%BF%E3%83%9E%E3%83%A1",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 108498894,
      "text": "ナガミハマナタマメ は、マメ科ナタマメ属の常緑匍匐性～つる性の多年生草本。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Canavalia rosea",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1327238073,
      "text": "Canavalia rosea is a species of flowering plant of the genus Canavalia in the pea family of Fabaceae, it has a pantropical and subtropical distribution in upper beaches, cliffs, and dunes. Common names include beach bean, bay bean, sea bean, greater sea bean, seaside jack-bean, coastal jack-bean, and MacKenzie bean."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Canavalia rosea",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 171145498,
      "text": "Canavalia rosea, comúnmente mate de costa, haba poroto de playa, haba de bahía, o haba poroto de MacKenzie, es una enredadera hallada en dunas tropicales y subtropicales."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Canavalia rosea",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 228196827,
      "text": "Canavalia rosea, nommé le Pois-bord-de-mer, Vonvon, Pois-cabrit aux Antilles françaises, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Fabaceae. C'est une liane rampante des hauts de plage des régions tropicales et subtropicales."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Canavalia rosea",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 51082183,
      "text": "O feijão-da-praia, é uma planta tropical, da família Fabaceae, amplamente cultivada nos países tropicais como cobertura verde. Sua associação, em nódulos radiculares com bactérias fixadoras de nitrogênio é natural, tendo sido demonstrado mesmo que, em certas regiões, a inoculação destas é indiferente."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Canavalia rosea",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 29691739,
      "text": "Canavalia rosea adalah spesies tanaman berbunga dari genus Canavalia dalam famili kacang polong Fabaceae, ia memiliki distribusi pantropis dan subtropis di pantai bagian atas, tebing, dan bukit pasir. Nama umum termasuk kacang pantai, kekara pantai, atau kekara laut."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Canavalia rosea § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1327238073,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Young seeds and pods are edible, especially after boiling. The flowers can be made into a spice.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Canavalia rosea § Utilisation",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea#Utilisation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 228196827,
        "heading": "Utilisation",
        "text": "Les Canavalia contiennent de nombreux toxiques : lectines, cyanides, alcaloïdes. Les graines sont comestibles.\nOn ne connait pas d'usage alimentaire de C. rosea dans les Amériques.\nEn Malaisie, les fleurs seraient consommées",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "pt": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Canavalia rosea § Usos",
        "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea#Usos",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 51082183,
        "heading": "Usos",
        "text": "O feijão-da-praia (Canavalia rosea) supostamente quando fumada pode agir como um fraco psicoativo; é utilizado como substituto do tabaco nos rituais tribalisticos que utilizam cannabinoides, opio, entre outras.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "id": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (id): Canavalia rosea § Penggunaan",
        "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_rosea#Penggunaan",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 29691739,
        "heading": "Penggunaan",
        "text": "Biji dan polong muda dapat dimakan terutama setelah direbus. Bunganya bisa dijadikan bumbu.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
